{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531562-v20-thaumaturgy-paths-with-a-single-effect-and-difficulty-rating","id":1531562,"title":"V20 Thaumaturgy Paths with a single effect and difficulty rating","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-26T16:48:55-08:00","id":1531562,"title":"V20 Thaumaturgy Paths with a single effect and difficulty rating","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> The general description of paths indicates:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thaumaturgical Paths p. 213 V20 Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each time the character invokes one of the powers<br /> of a Thaumaturgical path, the thaumaturge\u2019s player<br /> must spend a blood point and make a <b>Willpower roll<br /> against a difficulty equal to the power\u2019s level +3</b>. Only<br /> one success is required to invoke a path\u2019s effect \u2014 path<br /> levels, not successes, govern the power of blood magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Paths mention:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lure of Flames p. 218 V20 Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Individual descriptions are not provided for each<br /> level of this path \u2014 fire is fire, after all</b> (including po-<br /> tentially causing frenzy in other vampires witnessing<br /> it).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Movement of the Mind p. 220 V20 Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like The Lure of Flames,<b> individual power levels are<br /> not provided for this path</b> \u2014 consult the chart below<br /> to see how much weight a thaumaturge may control.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> So what difficulties do I use? Based on the rating of the effect? So if I want to move a 500 kilo thing, I roll at difficulty 8, but a pen is difficulty 4?<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Fixing grammar, and text in the start of the message. 02-26-2024, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-26T20:31:42-08:00","id":1531578,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you just check which level you need to use to do what you're trying to do.<br /> Lifting something light within the amount given for level 1 will be difficulty 4; something requiring the amount mentioned for level 5, difficulty 8.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T15:26:31-08:00","id":1531705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1531562-v20-thaumaturgy-paths-with-a-single-effect-and-difficulty-rating?p=1531578#post1531578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, you just check which level you need to use to do what you're trying to do.<br /> Lifting something light within the amount given for level 1 will be difficulty 4; something requiring the amount mentioned for level 5, difficulty 8.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for clarifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}